sequential/test-dgram-bind-shared-ports.js: cross-module integration: forks cluster workers and asserts the cluster UDP handle broker's exclusive/non-exclusive port-sharing policy; that broker is outside the dgram profile
sequential/test-dgram-implicit-bind-failure.js: language non-goal: replaces lookup and inspects the pending queue through Node's private symbol-keyed socket state; local/implicit-bind-failure-static.js retains the public error-monitor and repeated-send behavior
internet/test-dgram-broadcast-multi-process.js: cross-module integration: forks three child processes and verifies broadcast delivery across IPC-managed process lifetimes; spawned children cannot be substituted with this in-process dgram profile
internet/test-dgram-multicast-multi-process.js: cross-module integration: coordinates multicast membership and packet delivery across forked child processes; spawned children cannot be substituted with this in-process dgram profile
internet/test-dgram-multicast-set-interface-lo.js: cross-module integration: forks six listener processes and coordinates multicast-interface changes through IPC; spawned children cannot be substituted with this in-process dgram profile
internet/test-dgram-multicast-ssm-multi-process.js: cross-module integration: verifies IPv4 source-specific multicast across forked listener processes; spawned children cannot be substituted with this in-process dgram profile
internet/test-dgram-multicast-ssmv6-multi-process.js: cross-module integration: verifies IPv6 source-specific multicast across forked listener processes; spawned children cannot be substituted with this in-process dgram profile
known_issues/test-dgram-bind-shared-ports-after-port-0.js: upstream known issue: this file intentionally encodes an unresolved cluster port-zero sharing failure and is not a passing behavioral oracle
parallel/test-child-process-dgram-reuseport.js: cross-module integration: forks a child and asserts reusePort behavior across two process-local UDP handle tables; spawned children cannot be substituted with this in-process dgram profile
parallel/test-child-process-fork-dgram.js: cross-module integration: transfers a live UDP socket over child-process IPC and verifies shared-handle delivery; native handle serialization belongs to child_process rather than standalone dgram
parallel/test-cluster-child-index-dgram.js: cross-module integration: forks a cluster worker and verifies the cluster UDP broker's child-index bookkeeping across repeated binds
parallel/test-cluster-dgram-1.js: cross-module integration: distributes packets over one brokered UDP handle shared by multiple cluster workers
parallel/test-cluster-dgram-2.js: cross-module integration: coordinates explicitly bound UDP senders through cluster IPC and worker disconnect lifecycle
parallel/test-cluster-dgram-bind-fd.js: cross-module integration: passes a raw UDP descriptor through the cluster broker and binds that descriptor in multiple workers
parallel/test-cluster-dgram-ipv6only.js: cross-module integration: verifies brokered IPv6-only UDP bind policy inside a cluster worker
parallel/test-cluster-dgram-reuse.js: cross-module integration: verifies two UDP sockets sharing a port under the cluster worker handle broker
parallel/test-cluster-dgram-reuseport.js: cross-module integration: verifies reusePort bypasses cluster._getServer inside a forked cluster worker
parallel/test-cluster-disconnect-unshared-udp.js: cross-module integration: coordinates unbound and bound UDP resources through cluster worker disconnect accounting
test-dgram-bind-socket-close-before-cluster-reply.js: cross-module integration: exercises a cluster worker closing its socket while cluster._getServer is returning a shared UDP handle; the cluster handle broker is outside the dgram profile
test-dgram-cluster-bind-error.js: cross-module integration: replaces cluster._getServer to inject a shared-handle bind failure and inspects the private _bindState; neither the cluster broker nor that private state is a dgram public surface
test-dgram-cluster-close-during-bind.js: cross-module integration: replaces cluster._getServer and the brokered handle's close method while a worker bind is pending; the standalone close-during-bind behavior is covered separately
test-dgram-cluster-close-in-listening.js: cross-module integration: forks cluster workers and exercises brokered UDP-handle teardown; closing an ordinary dgram socket from listening is covered by test-dgram-close-in-listening.js
test-dgram-close-during-bind.js: language non-goal: mutates the lookup and bind methods through Node's private symbol-keyed socket state; test-dgram-bind-socket-close-before-lookup.js covers the public close-before-lookup-completes behavior
test-dgram-close.js: language non-goal: captures Node's private symbol-keyed native handle solely to inspect its fd after public close; public close ordering and callbacks are covered by the other upstream close tests
test-dgram-create-socket-handle-fd.js: internal API: exercises deprecated dgram._createSocketHandle with raw UDPWrap/TCPWrap objects obtained from internalBinding; that cluster handle-construction primitive is not part of the typed public dgram surface
test-dgram-create-socket-handle.js: internal API: imports internal/dgram._createSocketHandle and asserts raw UDPWrap identity and fd fields; the profile intentionally exposes typed Socket objects rather than Node's private native-wrap objects
test-dgram-exclusive-implicit-bind.js: cross-module integration: requires cluster workers' non-exclusive explicit binds to share one UDP handle while implicit exclusive binds remain per-worker; that behavior belongs to Node's cluster handle broker
test-dgram-recv-error.js: language non-goal: invokes onmessage directly through Node's private symbol-keyed native handle to inject an impossible receive result; ordinary receive delivery and public recvmsg error shaping are implemented without exposing that handle
test-dgram-send-error.js: language non-goal: replaces lookup and send through Node's private symbol-keyed native handle; local/send-lookup-error-static.js covers both public custom-lookup error paths and test-dgram-msgsize.js covers native send error metadata
test-dgram-socket-buffer-size.js: language non-goal: its first assertion requires Node's private kIsNodeError symbol and own getter/setter descriptors solely to match util.inspect output; local/socket-buffer-size-static.js retains every public buffer-size behavior with ordinary typed error fields
test-dgram-unref-in-cluster.js: cross-module integration: forks a cluster worker and observes cluster/process active-resource accounting for a brokered UDP handle; ordinary dgram ref and unref behavior is covered by test-dgram-ref.js and test-dgram-unref.js
